-- title:
--   Residue discs from an affine chart: disjointness, cusps, equivariance
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$ and a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ in its nonunits, a finset $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\ q\ M'$, an element $s \in W$, the inclusion $\mathrm{hle}$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$, subfields $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and $K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $k_0$, and a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ cut out by $A$, assumed a discrete valuation ring with $\mathfrak{m}_{A_b} = (\varpi_b)$. With $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ viewed as a $k_0$-algebra, let $F_0$ be an intermediate field, $B$ a subring of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ carrying an $A_b$-algebra structure, containing the Laurent expansion $j_q$ and stable under all $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; let $FSS$ be a field over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and $R$ a regular prolongation of $A$ to $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ with residue field $FSS$, with $B \subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$ and $FSS$ the field of fractions of the residues of $B$. Let $N$ be the finset of places $Q$ of $FSS$ omitting some residue of $B$, assumed stable under the residue automorphisms $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ attached to level automorphisms $\tau$ preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and let $S_Q$, $\varphi_Q : A_b[X] \to S_Q$, $\chi_Q : S_Q \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ satisfy, for $Q \notin N$, the list $\mathrm{hS}$ (summarised here): $S_Q$ contains the image of $A_b$ and equals the localisation $\{g/h : g,h \in B,\ \bar h(Q) \ne 0\}$ with fraction field $k_0(K_b) \sqcup F_0$; $\varphi_Q$ sends constants to their images, is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type, with $\chi_Q \circ \varphi_Q$ the residue map on constants and $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q X) = 0$; $\ker \chi_Q$ is the maximal ideal of the local ring $S_Q$; $S_Q \subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$, with maximal ideal cut out by divisibility by $\varphi_Q(C\,\varpi_b)$, residues of $S_Q$ lying in $Q$ and reducing to $\chi_Q$, and $\mathrm{ord}_Q$ of the residue of $\varphi_Q X$ equal to $1$. Finally let $D_Q$ consist of the rational places $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that every $f \in S_Q$ lies in $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$, and $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is $<1$ precisely when $\chi_Q f = 0$. The conclusion has three parts: for $Q, Q' \notin N$, a common member of $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$ forces $Q = Q'$; for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_Q$, $\mathrm{ord}_P(j) \ge 0$; and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma$ ($\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$) preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and every place $Q$, one has $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau \cdot Q \in N$ iff $Q \in N$ (a restatement of the hypothesis on $N$), and, for $Q \notin N$, $\{P : \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D_Q\} = D_{R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau \cdot Q}$.
--
--   This supplies the three riders of the smooth-point half of the semistable-model analysis at a supersingular point: distinct smooth points have disjoint residue discs, no cusp lies in such a disc, and the ends and discs are permuted compatibly by the level automorphisms. It is used by the statements assembling the supersingular discrete valuation rings and the base smooth-point stalks from an affine chart.
